// Request volume and latency, bucketed by hour.
//
// percentile(duration, 95) rather than avg(): an average hides the slow tail, and on this
// deployment the tail is the interesting part. F1 has no Always On, so the app cold-starts after
// idling, and the serverless database resumes from auto-pause on top of that. Those show up as
// a p95 far above the median rather than as a shifted average.
requests
| where timestamp > ago(24h)
| summarize
    count(),
    median = percentile(duration, 50),
    p95 = percentile(duration, 95)
  by bin(timestamp, 1h), name
| order by timestamp desc, count_ desc
